  "result": "I added `parseRange` to `src/cli/range.ts`, with tests in `test/cli/range.test.ts`, and committed it as f8fd99b. `npm run fast` passes (biome, boundaries, tsc and 18 related tests).\n\n`parseRange('1-3,5')` returns `[1, 2, 3, 5]`. It accepts spaces around numbers and dashes. It throws an error on malformed parts (`''`, `a`, `1-`, `1,,2`, `-3`) and on descending ranges like `3-1`. You didn't specify error behavior, so I chose to throw rather than return a partial result.\n\nThe repo also has a rule test that requires every test file to have an entry in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`. I added `'test/cli/range.test.ts': 0.1` there. That value is my guess, copied from the other small tests, not a CI-measured weight.\n\nThe commit title and `Ticket:` trailer use t-4kv2nz2, per KRN-11. I haven't pushed or opened a PR.",
